{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"2da475afdd929400b6eaf47fb0ff9ba561c877b73ae5398daff34e5ff9351558","slug":"intro.what-is-eeio","location":"/intro/what-is-eeio.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"What is an EEIO model?","authors":[{"nameParsed":{"literal":"Cornerstone Sustainability Data Initiative","given":"Cornerstone Sustainability Data","family":"Initiative"},"name":"Cornerstone Sustainability Data Initiative","id":"contributors-myst-generated-uid-0"}],"github":"https://github.com/cornerstone-data/eeio-docs","keywords":["EEIO","MRIO","input-output","emission factors","Scope 3","greenhouse gas"],"source_url":"https://github.com/cornerstone-data/eeio-docs/blob/main/intro/what-is-eeio.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/cornerstone-data/eeio-docs/edit/main/intro/what-is-eeio.md","thumbnail":"/eeio-docs/pr-preview/pr-28/build/eeio-overview-261440001bcb53d56e21a6c2dd6b9ed3.svg","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"what-is-eeio.md","url":"/eeio-docs/pr-preview/pr-28/build/what-is-eeio-800047a966541db05de11cf88f54e9f7.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"admonition","kind":"tip","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Summary","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"AdR810cL5Z"}],"key":"yKkG1AMNkZ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"An environmentally-extended input-output (","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"MN2YrEeDCK"},{"type":"crossReference","label":"EEIO","identifier":"term-eeio","children":[{"type":"text","value":"EEIO","key":"Eu4cZuCbd0"}],"kind":"definitionTerm","template":"{name}","resolved":true,"html_id":"term-eeio","remote":true,"url":"/reference/glossary","dataUrl":"/reference.glossary.json","key":"S7c6LqF9w8"},{"type":"text","value":") model combines data of how outputs produced by sectors in an economy serve as inputs for other sectors along with environmental attributes of each sector. When the economic data is extended with environmental data this way, such as with GHG emissions, the resulting model can produce emission factors that represent the GHG emissions across a whole supply chain per dollar spent on a sector’s products.","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"xD4bp4ouQr"}],"key":"YCuBPAW3fH"}],"key":"TSZDgYw1jW"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/eeio-docs/pr-preview/pr-28/build/eeio-overview-261440001bcb53d56e21a6c2dd6b9ed3.svg","alt":"Two grey boxes on the left feed arrows into a central box labeled EEIO model. The upper box, input-output tables, shows a small grid of cells and is described as dollars flowing between sectors and to final users, with the letters V, U, A, and L. The lower box, environmental extension, shows a row of shaded cells labeled CO₂, CH₄, and so on, and is described as greenhouse gases emitted by each sector, with the letters E, B, and C. The EEIO model traces emissions through every round of suppliers. An arrow from it leads to a highlighted box, emission factors D and N, in kilograms of CO₂e per dollar of purchases, by sector and country.","key":"XSkzsiYBrd","urlSource":"../figures/diagrams/eeio-overview.svg"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"fig-eeio-overview","identifier":"fig-eeio-overview","html_id":"fig-eeio-overview","enumerator":"1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"Ko7pM6xyYc"},{"type":"text","value":"1","key":"vLXmrdnSUW"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"BsyMhqiilc"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"TDOKMdWTnY"},{"type":"text","value":"An EEIO model combines input-output tables with an environmental extension to produce emission factors.","position":{"start":{"line":12,"column":1},"end":{"line":12,"column":1}},"key":"RpyAYowrkz"}],"key":"ScF68KtI0u"}],"key":"S0PBXC9i8z"}],"label":"fig-eeio-overview","identifier":"fig-eeio-overview","enumerator":"1","html_id":"fig-eeio-overview","key":"kMoPMyttOc"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where EEIO comes from","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"key":"kUw34Wsgml"}],"identifier":"where-eeio-comes-from","label":"Where EEIO comes from","html_id":"where-eeio-comes-from","implicit":true,"key":"hKtwVUqWnW"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"EEIO grew out of economic input-output analysis when economist Wassily Leontief added the pollution generated by each sector to his model of the economy ","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"e9MKxk1KPO"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"cite","identifier":"leontiefenvironmentalrepercussionseconomic1970","label":"leontiefEnvironmentalRepercussionsEconomic1970","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":155},"end":{"line":17,"column":202}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Leontief, 1970","key":"t4eQSFeV2w"}],"enumerator":"1","key":"HlYyTarplG"}],"key":"sA3E9pBqHL"},{"type":"text","value":", and it has been a basis for carbon footprinting of nations, organizations, and products over the last few decades ","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"xS9e0fmvX2"},{"type":"citeGroup","kind":"parenthetical","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"cite","identifier":"minxinputoutputanalysiscarbon2009","label":"minxInputOutputAnalysisCarbon2009","kind":"parenthetical","posi